human-copy's text is our own, written from the sources listed in
skills/human-copy/references/sources.md. Three of them shaped it enough to
credit here.

"Signs of AI writing" by Wikipedia's WikiProject AI Cleanup
(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Signs_of_AI_writing), CC BY-SA 4.0.
The vocabulary lists by model era, the signs of human writing and the
ineffective indicators in skills/human-copy/references/ are adapted from it,
and those passages stay under CC BY-SA 4.0.

tropes.fyi by Ossama Chaib (https://tropes.fyi), CC BY 4.0. Several entries in
skills/human-copy/references/tells.md take their names and example phrases from
its tropes.md.

humanizer by blader (https://github.com/blader/humanizer), MIT licence. The
grouping of tells by cause and the "wrong reader" entry follow its lead.
